    verificationBasis: 'USDA FSIS Safe Minimum Internal Temperatures chart lists 160°F for ground beef, pork, veal, and lamb. The 375°F/55–70 minute window reflects standard free-form meatloaf technique for a 2 lb loaf shaped roughly 2 inches tall; a pan-baked loaf of the same weight sits deeper and can need 70–80 minutes, and a leaner turkey mixture at the same shape finishes 5–10 minutes sooner.',
