    technicalDeepDive: 'Dry beans store their starch inside cells walled off by pectin, and that wall has to soften before water can fully penetrate the interior; on LOW, a slow cooker never quite sustains the near-boiling energy an unsoaked bean needs to hydrate all the way through within a single day, which is why this recipe runs HIGH instead. The smoked ham hock contributes rendered fat and dissolved collagen that coat the beans as they cook, giving the pot liquor body without adding starch of its own. Onion and bay steep their aromatics into the broth through slow diffusion, the way tea steeps in hot water.',
    keywords: ['how long to slow cook great northern beans', 'great northern beans slow cooker time', 'slow cooker beans from dry', 'crockpot beans no soak', 'unsoaked beans slow cooker'],
    metaDescription: 'How long to cook great northern beans in the slow cooker from dry: 5–6 hours on HIGH, unsoaked, skimming once at the 90-minute mark.',
