    proTip: 'Strip is leaner than ribeye — the same 5°F overshoot that a ribeye hides under its fat cap turns a strip grey and dry. Pull at 125°F, not "when it looks done"; the exterior is misleading on a hot grate because the outer inch cooks well past the target before the centre gets there.',
