    technicalDeepDive: 'A 45-minute dry brine gives salt time to draw juice out and dissolve surface myosin, leaving a drier surface than an unsalted steak. That matters on a 550°F grate because any residual surface water has to flash off as vapor, consuming energy as latent heat, before the surface can climb into the 280–330°F Maillard range; a pre-dried, blotted surface skips most of that stall and starts browning almost immediately. Strip loin also carries little fat to slow heat penetration, so its coagulation curve is steep — the four-to-five-minute per side timing exists to build a deep crust in the narrow window before the lean muscle beneath overshoots 130°F.',
    keywords: ['how long to grill ny strip steak', 'ny strip grill time', 'strip steak grill temperature', 'grilled strip steak medium rare', 'ny strip internal temp'],
    metaDescription: 'How long to grill NY strip steak: 550°F+ direct, 8–10 min to a 125°F pull. Why strip needs a tighter pull than ribeye.',
