    oilSprayRequired: false,
    proTip: 'The reverse sear only works if the steak surface is bone-dry when it hits the cast iron — pull it from the oven at 115°F, blot every face with paper towels, and only then drop it in the ripping pan. Skip that blot and the surface moisture flashes to steam and the crust never forms; you get a grey, wet ribeye that would have been better cooked the normal way.',
