    technicalDeepDive: 'Pounding the breast to a uniform 3/4 inch removes the thickness gap that would otherwise let the thin tip finish before the thick lobe catches up. The spice crust isn\'t flat at a microscopic level, and wherever a raised granule of paprika or garlic touches the 550°F metal directly, that spot races past ordinary Maillard browning into outright char, while the lower-lying spots nearby, cushioned by a thinner film of butter, brown more gently. Breast meat has little of the connective tissue that buffers a thigh, so its safe window between undercooked and dry is narrow, which is why the precise pull-then-rest matters more here than on a fattier cut.',
    keywords: ['how long to cook blackened chicken cast iron', 'blackened chicken internal temp', 'cajun blackened chicken time', 'blackened chicken breast recipe', 'how to blacken chicken at home'],
