    verificationBasis: 'USDA MyPlate does not set an internal-temperature target for roasted potatoes — doneness is fork-tender interior with a caramelized cut face, so the internal-temp field is omitted rather than guessed (HR-2). The 425°F / 25–30 minute cut-face-down window reflects standard convection roasting for halved 1.5-inch waxy potatoes on a rimmed half-sheet (Cook\'s Illustrated "Best Roasted Baby Potatoes" and Serious Eats "Extra-Crispy Roasted Potatoes" both use the same cut-face-down protocol at the same temperature).',
    technicalDeepDive: 'Yukon Golds are a waxy, lower-starch potato, so the cut face holds its shape against direct pan heat instead of sloughing apart the way a starchier potato would. A half-sheet pan has very little thermal mass, so it dumps stored heat into that single contact point and recovers quickly, keeping the interface hot enough to cross into Maillard browning instead of stalling while surface moisture flashes off. The intact skin on top only sees radiant and convective oven air, so it wrinkles and blisters far more slowly than the pan-side face chars. That gap between the two surfaces is why the potato stays untouched for the entire cook.',
    keywords: ['how long to roast baby potatoes', 'sheet pan baby yukon gold potatoes', 'halved potatoes oven temperature', 'crispy roasted baby potatoes', 'baby potatoes 425'],
    metaDescription: 'How long to roast halved baby Yukon Gold potatoes on a sheet pan: 425°F (218°C) for 25–30 minutes, cut-face-down and never flipped.',
