    technicalDeepDive: 'Fresh Italian sausage is sealed inside a casing that behaves like a natural membrane, so the fat rendering out of the pork stays trapped against the meat instead of dripping away, which is part of why whole links stay juicier than split ones over the same 425°F exposure. The peppers and onions nearby hold far more free water than the casing does, so their surface vapor briefly slows char on the vegetable edges while the nearly dry casing is already crisping against the hot pan. Because pork only needs to clear 160°F throughout and a link is a narrow cylinder, conduction from below carries the center to temperature well before the casing scorches, which is why one flip at 15 minutes is enough to finish the far side.',
