    donenessCue: 'Down-facing cut faces are deep golden-brown to nearly black at the corners where the sugars have caramelized; a fork pierces the thickest cube with no resistance; edges that were touching the pan have a crackled crust while the tops are tender and slightly sweet-toasted.',
    oilSprayRequired: false,
    proTip: 'Cut the neck and the bulb separately, then cube — the neck is a solid column of flesh that cubes cleanly, while the bulb\'s hollow seed cavity needs to be halved and scooped first. Cubes from a single-pass whole-squash cut end up wildly uneven and roast unevenly (small ones scorch while big ones stay chalky). A hooked Y-peeler and a large chef\'s knife make the peel-and-cube of a 3 lb squash a 6-minute job instead of a wrestling match.',
    verificationBasis: 'USDA MyPlate does not set an internal-temperature target for roasted winter squash — doneness is fork-tender interior with a caramelized cut face, so the internal-temp field is omitted rather than guessed (HR-2). The 425°F / 25–30 minute window reflects standard high-heat convection roasting for 1-inch butternut cubes on a rimmed half-sheet (Cook\'s Illustrated "Best Roasted Butternut Squash" and Serious Eats "Roasted Butternut Squash" both land in this window for the same cut and pan).',
    technicalDeepDive: 'Butternut flesh is denser and more fibrous than potato, and it carries natural sugars that caramelize alongside the Maillard reaction once a cut face meets 425°F metal, which is part of why roasted squash reads sweeter than roasted potatoes from the same oven. Because the cubes are cut on all sides rather than halved with one flat face, only the single face resting on the pan gets that early conductive head start, so the flip at 18 minutes is what lets a second face reach the same color instead of leaving the other five pale. The dense flesh also softens at close to the same rate the exterior caramelizes, so the two finish together rather than one badly lagging the other.',
    keywords: ['how long to roast butternut squash', 'sheet pan butternut squash cubes', 'roasted butternut squash temperature', 'butternut squash 425 oven', 'crispy roasted squash'],
