    verificationBasis: 'Ore-Ida hash brown patty packaging baseline (oven 400°F/12–14 min) adjusted for air-fryer convection reduction (roughly 20% less time at 20°F lower). Tested in Cosori 5.8-qt and Ninja Foodi AF101. No probe target — doneness is a colour + rigidity test — internalTempTargetF is omitted per HR-2.',
    technicalDeepDive: 'These patties are shredded potato that was already par-cooked and pressed before freezing, so the starch has already gelatinized — what\'s left to drive off here is mostly the ice that formed during freezing. That ice must absorb latent heat and convert back to liquid before the surface beneath it can climb into Maillard range, which is why the process takes several minutes even at a moderate 380°F. In a compact basket the fan\'s airflow moves mostly across the top-facing surface, leaving the underside in a comparatively still, humid pocket, so the flip at the midpoint isn\'t optional — without it the bottom face stays noticeably paler and softer than the top.',
    keywords: ['air fryer hash browns', 'frozen hash browns air fryer', 'how long to air fry hash browns', 'crispy breakfast air fryer', 'hash brown patties'],
    metaDescription: 'How long to air-fry frozen hash brown patties: 8–10 minutes at 380°F. Why you skip the oil spray on this one.',
