    proTip: 'Frozen egg rolls in the air fryer beat the deep-fryer version for cleanup and beat the oven for crispiness — the convection dries the wrapper into shatter-crisp texture without soaking up excess oil. Serve with duck sauce and hot mustard within 5 minutes; they soften as they sit.',
    verificationBasis: 'USDA FSIS 165°F poultry safe minimum for chicken-filled rolls (safe for pork fillings too, as ground pork minimum is 160°F); Van\'s Kitchen and P.F. Chang\'s frozen egg roll packaging baseline (oven 400°F/10–12 min) adjusted for air-fryer.',
    technicalDeepDive: 'Unlike a corn tortilla, an egg roll wrapper is a thin wheat dough with a developed gluten network, and that network is what lets it puff into raised pockets instead of crisping flat — moisture trapped between layers turns to steam under the 380°F airflow and pushes outward against the stretchy dough before escaping. Underneath, the filling is a dense, frozen meat-and-cabbage mix that must absorb conducted heat slowly enough to thaw through before its coldest point reaches the 165°F mark USDA sets as safe for both pork and poultry. The wrapper, thin and low in mass, finishes browning ahead of the filling, so the midpoint flip keeps color even while the core catches up.',
