    technicalDeepDive: 'Tater tots are reconstituted from riced or shredded potato bound with starch, already broken down more than a whole-cut fry, so the gelatinized surface starch re-sets into a craggy, high-surface-area shell rather than a smooth crust. That irregular surface, with more exposed area per gram than a solid fry, is part of why the crust browns readily even as the compact interior, still dense with bound moisture, changes temperature far more slowly. Rack position matters too: closer to the upper element, tots reach Maillard range sooner than lower in the cavity, where the air carries more thermal mass to overcome first.',
    keywords: ['tater tots in oven', 'how long to bake tater tots', 'crispy tater tots frozen', 'tater tots temperature oven', 'tater tots vs air fryer'],
    metaDescription: 'How long to bake frozen tater tots in the oven: 25–30 minutes at 425°F, flipped once. Why spacing them out matters more than time.',
