    verificationBasis: 'USDA FSIS Poultry Safety Guidelines (165°F); Nordic Ware Half Sheet Roasting Reference.',
    technicalDeepDive: 'Breast is the leanest cut on the bird, with little intramuscular fat and almost no collagen to buffer it, so its fibers coagulate and squeeze out moisture on a narrow temperature window instead of the more forgiving curve a fattier cut gets — which is exactly why this recipe pulls early rather than cooking straight through to 165°F in the oven. Pulling at 160°F leaves the geometric center just under full coagulation, and heat still stored in the outer layers keeps conducting inward during the rest, carrying the core the rest of the way to 165°F with no added oven time. The lower 400°F setting compared to a thigh recipe also matters, since lean muscle has less fat to insulate it from a hotter external gradient.',
